From 9cc67482532f8497d44669f04288b9774db6fc3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:45:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor: buttons v3 (pause/resume only
 on/off, up/down set speed only, no engage floor)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Submodule-relative opendbc diff 2258c35a..0a19ee8a (integration-3 tip -> buttons-v3).

  hyundai: gas interceptor: buttons v3 — pause/resume is the only on/off; up/down only set speed; no engage floor

  Panda (hyundai_common.h): in gas-interceptor mode the SET/RES (down/up) falling edges no longer grant controls_allowed;
  the pause/resume (CruiseSwState 4) debounced release is the only grant (brake released for the whole press + debounce,
  MAIN off, no controls_allowed condition, gas allowed, no speed check). hyundai_setres_brake_seen removed. SCC
  openpilot-long (hyundai_longitudinal) keeps the upstream SET/RES edge grant.

  Car: CarState.update_button_enable in pedal mode = resumeCruise release only (accel/decelCruise never enable);
  carstate_ext SET/RES brake tracker removed; CP.minEnableSpeed = -1 (was 25 mph); the 25 mph number survives only as
  LOW_SPEED_FULL_GAS_SPEED, the speed at which the launch limit reaches the cap (throttle limit, not a floor).

  Tests: up/down never grant/disengage (panda + car), pause/resume at any speed, helpers engage via pause/resume,
  lockstep fuzz asserts every grant on both sides is a pause/resume release carried by resumeCruise.
